    <div class="section-tag">Foundation</div>
    <h2>1. What is Cybercrime?</h2>

    <p>Imagine you wake up one morning and discover that someone has emptied your bank account — not by breaking into a vault, but by sitting thousands of kilometres away at a computer. Or imagine a hacker leaking your private photos onto the internet without your consent. Or a foreign government planting malicious software into a nation's power grid. These aren't science-fiction scenarios — they happen every single day. These are all examples of <strong>cybercrime</strong>.</p>

    <p>A <strong>cybercrime</strong> is any illegal act where a computer, network, or digital device is either the <em>tool</em>, the <em>target</em>, or the <em>scene</em> of the crime. Cybercrime erases geographical boundaries; a criminal in one country can victimise millions of people in another country within seconds.</p>

