  <section id="s3">
    <div class="section-tag">Rationale</div>
    <h2>3. Why Cyber Laws Are Necessary</h2>

    <p>Before specific cyber laws existed, law enforcement had to try fitting digital crimes into old physical-world laws — like charging a hacker under "trespassing" laws meant for people entering someone's house. It was awkward, often ineffective, and left clear loopholes for criminals.</p>

    <h3>Core Reasons Cyber Laws are Essential</h3>

    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-num"></div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <strong>Legalising Digital Transactions</strong>
          <p>Before the IT Act 2000, electronic contracts and digital signatures had no legal standing in India. You could not sue someone for breaching an online agreement. Cyber laws changed this by giving electronic records the same legal weight as paper documents.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-num"></div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <strong>Defining and Punishing New Crimes</strong>
          <p>Traditional penal codes (like the Indian Penal Code, 1860) were designed for physical offences. They couldn't effectively handle hacking, spreading viruses, or sending malicious emails. Cyber laws specifically define these as crimes with appropriate punishments.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-num"></div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <strong>Protecting Citizens' Privacy &amp; Data</strong>
          <p>With billions of personal records stored digitally, cyber laws create obligations on companies to protect user data and penalise them if they fail, giving citizens a legal right to privacy.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-num"></div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <strong>Enabling Digital Governance (e-Governance)</strong>
          <p>Government services like Aadhaar, DigiLocker, PAN card applications, and filing income tax online all depend on the legal infrastructure created by cyber laws to be both valid and secure.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-num"></div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <strong>International Cooperation</strong>
          <p>Cybercrimes cross borders instantly. Having cyber laws aligned with international norms (like the Budapest Convention) helps India cooperate with other nations to investigate and prosecute criminals.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout warning">
      <div class="callout-title">⚠️ Real-World Consequence</div>
      <p>Without cyber laws, a hacker who broke into a bank's server could walk free because "breaking" into a digital system wasn't explicitly illegal under older laws. Cyber laws closed these gaps.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

