    <h3>Key Objectives of the IT Act 2000</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Provide legal recognition to <strong>electronic records</strong> and <strong>digital signatures</strong>.</li>
      <li>Facilitate <strong>e-governance</strong> and electronic filing with government departments.</li>
      <li>Define and penalise <strong>cybercrimes</strong> such as hacking, data theft, and spreading viruses.</li>
      <li>Establish the framework for <strong>Certifying Authorities</strong> (CAs) to issue digital certificates.</li>
      <li>Set up <strong>Cyber Appellate Tribunals</strong> for resolving cyber-related disputes.</li>
      <li>Amend existing laws (IPC, Evidence Act, RBI Act, Bankers' Book Evidence Act) to accommodate electronic records.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Structure of the IT Act 2000</h3>
