  <section id="s6">
    <div class="section-tag">Amendment</div>
    <h2>6. IT (Amendment) Act 2008</h2>

    <p>The original IT Act 2000, while groundbreaking, quickly showed its age as technology evolved rapidly. The <strong>Information Technology (Amendment) Act, 2008</strong> (ITAA 2008) was a major overhaul that came into effect on <strong>27th October 2009</strong>.</p>

    <h3>Major Changes Introduced by ITAA 2008</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cyber Terrorism (Section 66F):</strong> Added a specific provision with life imprisonment for cyber terrorism.</li>
      <li><strong>Identity Theft (Section 66C):</strong> Made identity theft an explicit criminal offence.</li>
      <li><strong>Child Pornography (Section 67B):</strong> Specifically criminalised child sexual abuse material (CSAM) online, separate from general obscenity.</li>
      <li><strong>Data Protection (Section 43A):</strong> Required "body corporates" (companies) handling sensitive personal data to maintain reasonable security practices. Failure to do so makes them liable to pay compensation.</li>
      <li><strong>Intermediary Liability Revised (Section 79):</strong> Clarified the "safe harbour" conditions more precisely for internet service providers and platforms.</li>
      <li><strong>Electronic Signature expanded:</strong> The definition of "digital signature" was expanded to "electronic signature" to accommodate newer authentication technologies beyond just PKI-based signatures.</li>
      <li><strong>Indian Computer Emergency Response Team (CERT-In):</strong> Formalised CERT-In as the nodal agency for cybersecurity incident response in India.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="callout case">
      <div class="callout-title">💡 Why the Amendment Was Needed</div>
      <p>Between 2000 and 2008, India saw a massive explosion in mobile phone usage, social media, online banking, and digital transactions. Crimes like phishing, SIM card fraud, cyberstalking, and online child abuse were rampant but not clearly covered. The 2008 amendment addressed these gaps directly.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

